From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flax <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Restore cache invalidation on firmware update

Upstream entity-manager drops /var/configuration/system.json when the
firmware version (/etc/os-release hash) changes, so a new image's
configurations are applied.  AMI's "SDR Preserve" change kept any
existing cache regardless of version, which left every upgraded BMC
running on configurations built from the previous image: fixes shipped
in fbtp.json never took effect until the cache was deleted by hand.

Restore the upstream condition.  Runtime edits made to entity-manager
objects (threshold values, fan PID settings) are therefore lost on a
firmware update, as they are on a factory reset.
---
 src/entity_manager.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/entity_manager.cpp b/src/entity_manager.cpp
--- a/src/entity_manager.cpp
+++ b/src/entity_manager.cpp
@@ -1378,7 +1378,7 @@ int main()
     });
     tryIfaceInitialize(entityIface);

-    if (fwVersionIsSame() || std::filesystem::exists(currentConfiguration))
+    if (fwVersionIsSame())
     {
         if (std::filesystem::is_regular_file(currentConfiguration))
         {
